1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:03,957
You ask a coding agent for one thing, and
then you wait.

2
00:00:04,307 --> 00:00:08,446
New ideas come up, but the agent can only
do one thing at a time.

3
00:00:08,796 --> 00:00:12,572
So you interrupt it, or you try to
remember everything yourself.

4
00:00:14,072 --> 00:00:15,779
symcc fixes that.

5
00:00:16,129 --> 00:00:17,985
It is a plugin for Claude Code.

6
00:00:18,335 --> 00:00:20,852
You talk to one lead, in your normal chat.

7
00:00:21,202 --> 00:00:25,433
The lead listens, writes your ideas down
on a shared task board,

8
00:00:25,433 --> 00:00:27,879
and splits big jobs into small tasks.

9
00:00:28,229 --> 00:00:31,643
Then workers pick up the tasks and do them
side by side.

10
00:00:31,993 --> 00:00:34,628
Each worker has its own copy of your code,

11
00:00:34,628 --> 00:00:38,457
so your own branch stays untouched until
something is merged.

12
00:00:39,957 --> 00:00:41,301
The board is simple.

13
00:00:41,651 --> 00:00:43,912
A task is in one of four places.

14
00:00:44,262 --> 00:00:46,246
Todo, doing, review, or done.

15
00:00:46,596 --> 00:00:50,735
You can see at a glance what is running,
what is waiting, and what needs you.

16
00:00:51,085 --> 00:00:53,047
And the lead is smart about order.

17
00:00:53,397 --> 00:00:56,427
If one task needs the result of another,
it waits.

18
00:00:56,777 --> 00:01:00,659
If two tasks change the same files, they
go one after the other.

19
00:01:01,009 --> 00:01:03,185
Everything else runs at the same time.

20
00:01:03,535 --> 00:01:05,477
You can change your mind any time.

21
00:01:05,827 --> 00:01:07,811
Just say, do task six first.

22
00:01:09,311 --> 00:01:11,593
Each worker gets its own git worktree.

23
00:01:11,943 --> 00:01:15,045
That is just a separate folder with its
own branch,

24
00:01:15,045 --> 00:01:17,234
so workers never step on each other.

25
00:01:17,584 --> 00:01:19,995
By default, three workers run at once.

26
00:01:20,345 --> 00:01:22,606
A task lists the files it may change.

27
00:01:22,956 --> 00:01:26,177
If a worker changes anything else, it is
not merged.

28
00:01:26,527 --> 00:01:28,981
Before any merge, your tests must pass.

29
00:01:29,331 --> 00:01:32,701
If they fail, a new worker sees the error
and tries again.

30
00:01:33,051 --> 00:01:34,886
You choose how much to trust it.

31
00:01:35,236 --> 00:01:39,247
In auto mode, a finished task that passes
is merged right away.

32
00:01:39,597 --> 00:01:42,365
In review mode, you look at the changes
first,

33
00:01:42,365 --> 00:01:44,653
then approve, or reject with a reason.

34
00:01:45,003 --> 00:01:49,461
And if a worker has a question, the task
waits under a heading called needs you.

35
00:01:49,811 --> 00:01:51,646
You answer, and it goes on.

36
00:01:53,146 --> 00:01:54,426
Then there are scouts.

37
00:01:54,776 --> 00:01:57,443
A scout is a helper that wakes up on a
timer.

38
00:01:57,793 --> 00:02:01,291
It looks for bugs, missing tests, or old
dependencies.

39
00:02:01,641 --> 00:02:04,308
It can only read, never change your files.

40
00:02:04,658 --> 00:02:07,325
When it finds something, it reports to the
lead.

41
00:02:07,675 --> 00:02:11,515
The lead turns the finding into a task,
and a worker picks it up.

42
00:02:11,865 --> 00:02:14,809
So the work keeps moving, even when you
step away.

43
00:02:16,309 --> 00:02:18,101
Let us follow one request.

44
00:02:18,451 --> 00:02:21,992
You type, add a search command, and make
the errors friendlier.

45
00:02:22,342 --> 00:02:24,006
The lead makes three tasks.

46
00:02:24,356 --> 00:02:25,593
The search index.

47
00:02:25,943 --> 00:02:28,695
The search command, which waits for the
index.

48
00:02:29,045 --> 00:02:30,496
And the friendlier errors.

49
00:02:30,846 --> 00:02:33,598
The index and the errors start now, in
parallel.

50
00:02:33,948 --> 00:02:37,191
Each worker builds in its own copy, and
the tests run.

51
00:02:37,541 --> 00:02:39,525
The first task lands in review.

52
00:02:39,875 --> 00:02:43,565
You open it, see the changes, and say,
approve task one.

53
00:02:43,915 --> 00:02:46,390
It merges, and the search command starts.

54
00:02:46,740 --> 00:02:48,276
You never typed a command.

55
00:02:48,626 --> 00:02:49,735
You just talked.

56
00:02:51,235 --> 00:02:55,843
symcc is free and open source, under the
MIT license.

57
00:02:56,193 --> 00:02:57,857
You need Claude Code and git.

58
00:02:58,207 --> 00:03:03,114
Install it as a plugin with one command,
and the steps are in the project's page.

59
00:03:03,464 --> 00:03:06,963
Set your test command, ask for something,
and watch the board.

60
00:03:07,313 --> 00:03:08,422
symcc.

61
00:03:08,772 --> 00:03:10,479
Many agents, one board.
